From freebsd-alpha  Wed Feb 21 18:52:38 2001
From: Andrew Gallatin <gallatin () cs ! duke ! edu>
Date: Wed, 21 Feb 2001 18:52:38 +0000
To: freebsd-alpha
Subject: Re: Netscape broken on -CURRENT
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=freebsd-alpha&m=103030611407256


I think I've just fixed it.  The problem was caused by the new
optimized syscall return process.  In order to indicate to exception
return that we want all state restore after, for example, a signal, we
need to set FRAME_FLAGS to 0 -- this was missing from the osfulator.

Grab osf1_signal.c 1.7 for the fixed version.

Thanks again for pointing this out!

Drew


